{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/683305-wodgotham-com-is-the-place-to-play","id":683305,"title":"WODGotham.com is the place to play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-30T11:08:52-07:00","id":683305,"title":"WODGotham.com is the place to play","content":"Hello all on Onyx Path,<br /> <br /> I wanted to share my experience for anyone who might be interested in joining a quality WoD chat.<br /> <br /> A little about me, I began on the site back in February. I had only played table top a handful of times and it was my first online RP experience.<br /> <br /> I was nervous of course, but wanted to jump right in and get going. To start was the sanctioning process, which while it took a little while( a little over a week) by the time it was finished I ended up loving my character even more. The STs did a very good job guiding me through the process.<br /> <br /> When I was finally able to go IC, I found a group of players who are very welcoming and friendly. There are even more now than when I started. PvP is a factor but no one holds grudges, its all part of the fun. The best part about getting in there for the first time was not knowing who is who, since it is a crossover game with mages, werewolves, vamps, and mortals all competing to exist in NYC.<br /> <br /> Being a new player does make it hard to figure out what I should be doing at times, but with all the resources available, (you could cruise the wiki into next week and still not read it all) and the way the STs help guide you, gets you up to speed pretty quick. Rather than just answer my questions, the ST have been using my storylines to send long lasting messages and lessons, whether I fail or succeed I move forward a little more knowledgeable.<br /> <br /> So If like me you are new to RP or are a veteran who knows what the deal is, you should check us out.